      "reason": "DELIBERATE. Client ruling 2026-07-26 — the title always paints. schedule_tile was the only layout that structurally swallowed the required hero role: the rows owned the whole hero zone and a headline typed alongside the details painted nothing (measured pre-fix: hero reported dead in 18/18 of its archetype x format x size-step cells). The title now takes a band at the top of the zone and the rows take the rest. The fingerprint fixture carries BOTH a headline and a subtext, so all six schedule_tile cells now paint a title they previously omitted. Visually reviewed on canvas in all 6 formats (scratchpad/sched-before-*.png vs sched-after-*.png). Every other cell is byte-identical: 138/144 unchanged."
